    alignment: "The video's proposition that investigators cannot determine whether the subject is a threat or a revelation — and that the subject is simultaneously both — is documented across the McLean archive's dual reception history: 25+ domestic agencies framing the same archive as a threat requiring 14 hospitalisations and $11.5M suppression; the ICC and UNHCR framing the same archive as the evidentiary basis for Article 7 international criminal review. Corroborated across Isaiah's cornerstone/stumbling-stone dual-nature archetype and Jung's enantiodromia (extreme suppression producing the conditions for its own reversal through the archive it generated).",
