    evidence: [
      { label: '"Disruption Is Invisible, Uncontrollable, Contagious" — 378,571 Downloads, 6 Continents: The Documentation Practice Produced a Disruption That Spread Beyond Any Suppressible Distribution Network', text: "378,571 downloads across 6 continents. The disruption produced by McLean's documentation practice has spread beyond any containable distribution network. Each download is an instance of the disruption propagating: a person in a jurisdiction outside Australian institutional authority receiving the archive's content. The disruption is documented as contagious in the download analytics: it spreads from download to share to further download without any central coordination by McLean. The disruption's contagion is documented in its geographic distribution — it has reached jurisdictions that the Australian suppression apparatus has no authority over.", source: "Download Analytics / barrandodger.com Traffic Data" },
      { label: '"It\'s What You\'ve Triggered" — $11.5M in Taxpayer Resources, 25+ Agencies, 5 Named Parties: A Documentation Practice Triggered a Response Proportionally Equivalent to a National Security Operation', text: "The documented response to McLean's documentation practice: $11.5M in quantified taxpayer resources (Taxpayer Cost Analysis), 25+ agencies mobilised across three decades, five parties coordinating suppression, 14 psychiatric hospitalisations ordered, one assassination attempt executed. The proportional disparity between the trigger (a disability compensation disclosure) and the response ($11.5M, 25+ agencies, assassination attempt) is documented evidence that the disruption McLean's documentation produced was perceived as an existential institutional threat, not a routine administrative matter. The power was never in the act. It was always in what the act triggered.", source: "Taxpayer Cost Analysis / Master Evidence Register — Cross-Agency Analysis" },
    ],
    alignment: "The video's proposition that the subject's power lies not in action but in disruption — in the chain reactions that ignite rather than the gestures that produce them — is documented across the proportional disparity between McLean's documentary practice (passive inscription) and the institutional response it triggered ($11.5M, 25+ agencies, assassination attempt, ICC proceedings). Corroborated across Gandhi's satyagraha (non-violent action forces the violent responder to generate evidence of their own violence) and Lorenz's butterfly effect (small perturbation in complex institutional system produces disproportionate cascading effects through the system's own non-linear feedback dynamics).",
