    proposition: "Every label the suppression apparatus applied to McLean became a more accurate description of the apparatus itself than of McLean. 'Delusional' — applied to McLean while the clinical institutions maintained clinical labels contradicted by documentary evidence: the documented delusion was institutional, not McLean's. 'Vexatious' — applied to McLean while 25+ agencies processed legitimate whistleblower disclosures through circular referral without substantive engagement: the documented vexatious conduct was the circular referral system's, not McLean's. 'Threat' — applied to McLean while an assassination attempt was being coordinated: the documented threat was the assassination conspirators', not McLean's. 'Lacks insight' — applied to McLean while clinical assessors lacked access to the documentary archive that would have changed every assessment they issued: the documented lack of insight was the assessors', not McLean's. In each case, the label applied to McLean is more precisely described as a characterisation of the labelling apparatus's own conduct. McLean is the moving mirror: every attempt to define him produced a portrait of the definer.",
    verdict: "CORROBORATED",
