    alignment: "The video's proposition that the subject is a moving mirror — that every label applied to them reveals the labeller's own conduct more accurately than the subject's — is documented in the precise cross-reference of every institutional characterisation applied to McLean against the documentary record: 'delusional' (institutional delusion documented), 'vexatious' (institutional vexatiousness documented), 'lacks insight' (institutional lack of insight documented). The archive is the moving mirror: 2,301 documents, almost entirely generated by the institutions themselves, now assembled into a reflection the institutions cannot suppress. Corroborated across Lacan's mirror stage (projection reveals the projector's structure) and Dostoevsky's double (the institution finds its own portrait in the archive it generated).",
