    title: '"They don\'t want truth. They want control."',
    proposition: "The truth of McLean's disclosures was accessible to every agency in the 25+ agency network from the moment of each disclosure. The documentary evidence that corroborates 302 AI-analysed propositions with zero contradictions was available — because it was generated by the agencies themselves. The agencies did not lack access to the truth. They lacked the institutional capacity to acknowledge it. Acknowledging the truth of McLean's disclosures would require acknowledging the conduct the disclosures documented. The circular referral pattern is not the mechanism of truth-seeking. It is the mechanism of truth-avoidance: each referral preserved the referring agency's capacity to maintain that the disclosure was 'outside our jurisdiction' — a position that preserved control (no acknowledgment, no accountability) at the cost of truth (no engagement with the documentary evidence). $11.5M was deployed not to investigate the disclosures but to manage the discloser. 14 hospitalisations were not clinical truth-seeking about McLean's mental state — they were control instruments that preserved the institutional narrative against the documentary record. The video's eleventh principle is the operational doctrine of the suppression apparatus, documented in its own records.",
    verdict: "CORROBORATED",
    quote: '"They don\'t want truth. They want control. That\'s the real motive buried underneath their endless investigation... It isn\'t about learning who you are. It\'s about managing you, containing you, bending you into a version they can predict. Truth is dangerous to them because it isn\'t something they can own... control gives them comfort, order, authority. Truth, on the other hand, dismantles those illusions... Control dissolves where truth exists in its pure form."',
